        sequence: 'Keep the day intentionally narrow: travel from Ipoh to Batu Gajah or directly by road, make a pre-arranged last-mile transfer to Kellie’s Castle, spend the visit within open public areas, then return by the same confirmed ride. Add a town meal after reaching Ipoh. A separate tin-history museum, Gopeng adventure or cave-temple visit makes a different day and should not be fitted around a fixed train without confirmed opening and road timing.',
        boundary: 'The railway station, Batu Gajah town and the castle are distinct places. Do not walk the road shoulder between them or treat a map line as a pedestrian route. Follow the site’s barriers and posted instructions; do not enter closed upper levels or unsafe areas for a photo.',
        stages: [['Set the station or driver base', 'Compare current KTMB service to Ipoh and Batu Gajah for the actual date. If using rail, secure a named pickup from the correct station; if using a car from Ipoh, agree whether the driver waits or returns at a written time.'], ['Protect the last mile', 'Confirm travel time with the local driver on the day, allow for valley traffic and send the castle destination pin in advance. Save a return contact and agree what happens if the site visit runs late.'], ['Visit the castle deliberately', 'Check Tourism Malaysia’s current visitor notice or contact the site for operating hours, admission, last entry and closed areas before leaving Ipoh. Read the interpretation on the unfinished mansion and its historical context; label supernatural anecdotes as legend, not documented fact.'], ['Return before the connection', 'Leave enough road margin to reach your driver, station or Ipoh base well before the next train. If the pickup fails or the site is closed, return to Ipoh’s walkable Old Town and railway/civic quarter rather than searching for a roadside transfer.']],
        risks: [['Last-mile gap', 'KTMB’s station list is not an attraction transfer. A train ticket alone does not solve the road connection; arrange both directions before departure.'], ['Unconfirmed visitor details', 'Tourism Malaysia’s castle page could not be inspected in this review, and no reliable current fee, opening calendar or last-entry time was verified. Confirm with the site directly; do not book a tight same-day rail return.'], ['Heat, rain and uneven steps', 'The castle visit involves an exposed hilltop setting and old construction. Wear grippy shoes, take water, follow staff and barriers, and keep a wet-weather return plan.']],
        duration: 'Allow at least a half day once the road transfer and site visit are included; use a full day if you need a flexible driver or are connecting by rail. Exact visit length depends on current access and your pace, not a fixed online estimate.',
