        lead: 'The core is compact enough for a half-day walk, but the route changes character between Gaya Street, the uphill Atkinson Clock Tower and the harbor edge. Treat the Sunday market as a dated weekly opportunity, not a daily attraction, and keep a road-ride option ready for heat or rain.',
        orientation: 'A Gaya Street or central-waterfront room makes this chapter easiest on foot. The Sabah Tourism Board\'s heritage walk names Australia Place, Atkinson Clock Tower, the Sabah Tourism Building, Jesselton Hotel, the Malaysia Monument, the War Memorial and the City Council Building; it is a longer route than a short market browse. Check current access and street crossings before joining the stops.',
        arrival: 'From Kota Kinabalu International Airport (KKIA), book a metered taxi or e-hailing ride to the exact hotel entrance; no current fare or drive-time estimate is asserted here. On foot, pin Gaya Street and the exact heritage stop rather than asking for the general waterfront. Sabah Tourism lists buses and e-hailing, but use its live stop and service information for the return.',
        sequence: 'Start in the Gaya Street market or shop grid, climb toward Atkinson Clock Tower only if the slope and weather suit the group, select one heritage interior, then finish at the named Jesselton Point Waterfront or Central Market edge. Use a short ride between legs when crossings, heat or mobility make the walk a poor trade.',
        boundary: 'The heritage walk is an editorial route through public streets, not permission to enter a building or a promise of step-free access. Market workers, customers and waterfront crews are not staged subjects; ask before close photographs and keep loading lanes clear.',
        routeLead: 'Follow a named old-town chain from Gaya Street to the hill marker and waterfront; the ride fallback is a deliberate leg, not a guessed bus number.',
        stages: [['Grid', 'Begin on Gaya Street in daylight. If your visit falls on Sunday, check the current Sunday Market notice before planning around stalls; on another day, use the same street for shops and food. Keep browsing out of vendor work space.'], ['Context', 'Walk uphill to Atkinson Clock Tower only if footing, heat and mobility suit the group. Continue to the Sabah Tourism Building or one confirmed heritage interior; take a ride instead of forcing the slope in rain.'], ['Market edge', 'Choose the Central Market or one named waterfront edge for a meal and a look at the working harbor. The market and pier are separate destinations, so pin the intended entrance.'], ['Sunset', 'Finish at Jesselton Point Waterfront only after checking the return ride or walk. Leave the bus, taxi or e-hailing pickup at a precise landmark rather than the generic word waterfront.']],
        risks: [['Heat and rain', 'The uphill marker and exposed waterfront are harder in strong sun or a sudden shower. Start early, carry water and shorten the hill leg when conditions change.'], ['Market and heritage access', 'The Sunday Market is day-specific; shop, memorial and building access can also change. Confirm the current notice and treat a closed interior as an exterior stop.'], ['Crossings and return', 'The city walk is not a single signed promenade. Check the next street crossing and a precise ride pickup before leaving the final waterfront block.']],
        duration: 'Reserve about half a day for a slow walk, food and one interior. This is an editorial estimate, not the duration of the full guided heritage product; add time for a ride or mobility break.',
        combine: 'Use it on an arrival or recovery day if the flight leaves daylight. Keep Sabah State Museum and Tanjung Aru as a separate road chapter, and do not start the walk just before a fixed island departure.',
        verify: 'Check the Sunday Market notice, heritage-stop access, METMalaysia city forecast and Sabah Tourism\'s current transit information; confirm the exact ride pickup and return.',
